name cili
# The Collaborative Interlingual Index (ili.ttl): one language-neutral concept per meaning, each a statement of its own,
#   <i1>	a	<Concept> ;
#   	skos:definition	"(usually followed by `to') having the necessary means or skill ..."@en ;
#   	dc:source	pwn30:00001740-a .
# A concept is its canonical identifier (i1), the node the highway's interlingual index lists; the WordNet 3.0 synset it
# was made from (dc:source, pwn30:00001740-a) is WordNet's key of it. What a concept is said to be (a Concept, an
# Instance) and its skos:definition are attested on it; a literal retains the language its definition is written in.
match ili.ttl
format turtle
tier statement by \n\n
where triple/subject matches ^i[0-9]+$

thing triple subject
thing rdf_literal value lang_tag
thing rdf_literal value
type lang_tag language
content *

# A Turtle predicate is an RDF property, of the source's own relation inventory (RDF 1.1 Turtle, 2.4: "The token 'a'
# in the predicate position of a Turtle triple represents the IRI http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type").
# These are predicate VALUES in the RDF statement, not XML tags or TSV column
# names. Retain the source's own relation inventory and the literal's language;
# do not replace either with English invented by a recipe author.
value - predicate
when predicate matches ^(a|skos:definition)$
relate property predicate to object_list
always

types ili "Interlingual index concept" triple
keyed ili triple subject
keyed ili triple property[predicate=dc:source]/object_list matching ^pwn30:(.*)$
